7	188,951,1575,1285	Fig. 7.	The curve of fig. 6 enlarged: a wavy line along the axis e f g h, one period divided into 12 numbered intervals with perpendiculars, beside a circle whose numbered points mark the corresponding positions.
8	150,2096,707,2237	Fig. 8.	A sawtooth curve marked 0, 5, 10: the displacement rises slowly and uniformly through nine intervals, then falls suddenly in the tenth, as with a violin string or a hammer lifted by a water-wheel.
